Implemented US-003.

Changed the resolver/codegen path so external schema analysis now stays on the shared `resolveRefGraph()` resolver path instead of falling back through a second `derefSpec()` pass. Key changes are in [ref-resolver.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/ref-resolver.ts), [ref-graph.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/ref-graph.ts), and [generate-types.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/codegen/src/typegen/generate-types.ts).

What changed:
- Added source metadata to resolver diagnostics and graph nodes: `sourceFilePath` / `sourcePointer`.
- Made internal refs inside external documents use file-qualified cache keys, avoiding cross-document cache/cycle ambiguity.
- Removed codegen’s `derefSpec()` fallback for external schema refs.
- Canonicalized nested external schema refs to absolute `filePath#pointer` identities before `schemaToTs()`, while preserving raw `$ref` overrides for entry-document refs.
- Preserved resolver diagnostic codes like `external-ref-read-failed` and `external-ref-pointer-not-found` in typegen diagnostics.
- Added coverage for cache reuse, source metadata, nested source-relative refs, and missing file/pointer diagnostics.
- Updated [spec.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/spec.md), [api-index.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/api-index.md), [todo.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/todo.md), and [.ralph-tui/progress.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/.ralph-tui/progress.md). Test counts now reflect codegen `467`, total `1587`.

Verification:
- `pnpm typecheck` passed.
- `pnpm --filter @oa-sdk/parser test` passed: 195 tests.
- `pnpm --filter @oa-sdk/codegen test` passed: 467 tests.
- `git diff --check` passed.
- `pnpm test` is blocked by the sandbox at mock-server integration tests with `listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1`; earlier packages through codegen passed before that stop.
- `pnpm schema:validate` is blocked by the same sandbox class at `tsx` IPC setup: `listen EPERM` on a temp pipe.
- Separate typia/playground tests also hit the same localhost listener restriction.

