80p' packages/parser/src/__tests__/ref-graph.test.ts\\\"\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:37:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,420p' packages/parser/src/__tests__/deref.test.ts\\\"\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:43:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"externalSpecPath|nestedExternalSpecPath|collisionSpecPath|\\\\\\\\.yaml#/components/...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:45:The implementation split is clear: parser `resolveRefGraph()` has its own traversal/cache, parser `derefSpec()` uses `DerefFolder` plus the ref graph pointer helper, and codegen `generateTypesFromSpec()` calls `analyzeExternalSchemaRefs()` which uses the ref graph and falls back to `derefSpec()` for external schemas. I’m going to add focused baseline tests around those exact boundaries and document the current gaps without changing runtime behavior. \\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:47:I’m making scoped changes now: a parser baseline file for graph and deref semantics, codegen typegen tests for external alias behavior, and internal docs that record the current path split and known resolver gaps.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:49:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc 'pnpm --filter @oa-sdk/parser test packages/parser/src/__tests__/resolver-baseline.test...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:65:> vitest run \\\"packages/parser/src/__tests__/resolver-baseline.test.ts\\\"\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:70:filter:  packages/parser/src/__tests__/resolver-baseline.test.ts\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:74:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc 'pnpm --filter @oa-sdk/parser exec vitest run src/__tests__/resolver-baseline.test.ts'\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:156: